ions","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/Hypergraph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A column is any set of vertices: empty columns and repeated columns are kept, and a graph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop is the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"loop a zero column; Godsil–Royle’s entry 2 is not a bit. A zero column would forget the loop.)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is the directed form; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation of the same hypergraphs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Both orientations are stored, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" stores its rows: n rows of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the row and column popcounts cached. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"the matrix is for dense or small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidence","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence belongs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. (","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s equality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/Hashable-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/hashable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/Hashable-Implementations","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Hashable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","